_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: VI.10
---
statement: To cut a given uncut straight line similarly to a given cut straight line.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *AB* be the given uncut straight line, and *AC* the straight line cut at the points *D* and *E,* and let them be so placed as to contain any angle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="340" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.10 diagram" src="propVI10.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.10",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;30,270",
            "B;point;free;250,270",
            "C;point;free;290,30",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A,C,90,200",
            "E;point;lineSlider;A,C,150,80",
            "F';point;parallelogram;B,C,D;0;0",
            "F;point;intersection;A,B,D,F'",
            "DF;line;connect;D,F",
            "G';point;parallelogram;B,C,E;0;0",
            "G;point;intersection;A,B,E,G'",
            "EG;line;connect;E,G",
            "K;point;parallelogram;D,F,B",
            "DK;line;connect;D,K",
            "H;point;intersection;D,K,E,G"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Join *CB,* and draw *DF* and *EG* through *D* and *E* parallel to *CB,* and draw *DHK* through *D* parallel to *AB.* [!just I.31]

Therefore each of the figures *FH* and *HB* is a parallelogram. Therefore *DH* equals *FG* and *HK* equals *GB.* [!just I.34]

Now, since the straight line *EH* is parallel to a side *CK* of the triangle *DCK,* therefore, proportionally, *DE* is to *EC* as *DH* is to *HK.* [!just VI.2]

But *DH* equals *FG,* and *HK* equals *GB,* therefore *DE* is to *EC* as *FG* is to *GB.* [!just V.7]

Again, since *DF* is parallel to a side *EG* of the triangle *AEG,* therefore, proportionally, *AD* is to *DE* as *AF* is to *FG.* [!just VI.2]

But it was also proved that *DE* is to *EC* as *FG* is to *GB,* therefore *DE* is to *EC* as *FG* is to *GB,* and *AD* is to *DE* as *AF* is to *FG.*

Therefore the given uncut straight line *AB* has been cut similarly to the given cut straight line *AC.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

In a sense, this proposition is a generalization of the last one @VI.9. Prop. VI.9 cut a line into two parts whose ratio was a given numerical ratio. This proposition cuts a line into two parts whose ratio is a given ratio of two other lines. Both propositions rely on @VI.2 as a basis to make any conclusion about the ratio of two lines.

#### Use of this construction

This proposition is not used later in the *Elements,* but it is a basic construction of geometry.
